WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.953
Structured notes turn browsing into reviewable work.

00:00:02.953 --> 00:00:07.843
Begin each case with the requirement, scope, authority, deadlines, and handling rules.

00:00:07.843 --> 00:00:12.326
Use dated entries that distinguish search actions, direct observations, source claims,

00:00:12.326 --> 00:00:14.364
questions, assumptions, and analytical judgments.

00:00:14.364 --> 00:00:19.255
A source log should record a stable source identifier, URL, page title,

00:00:19.255 --> 00:00:23.330
publisher or account, publication date when available, access timestamp, relevance,

00:00:23.330 --> 00:00:24.553
and preservation reference.

00:00:24.553 --> 00:00:29.036
This allows citations and later review even if the page changes.

00:00:29.036 --> 00:00:33.519
Store approved screenshots, archives, and downloaded public documents with consistent names.

00:00:33.519 --> 00:00:38.002
A useful convention may include date, source, short subject, and identifier.

00:00:38.002 --> 00:00:43.300
Avoid names such as screenshot one that lose meaning outside the analyst's desktop.

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:46.968
Separate raw collection from working material and final products.

00:00:46.968 --> 00:00:49.006
Preserve originals when integrity matters,

00:00:49.006 --> 00:00:51.858
record transformations such as translation or cropping,

00:00:51.858 --> 00:00:56.342
and link summaries or extracted facts back to the source identifier.

00:00:56.342 --> 00:01:01.232
Folder structures should be simple enough that another analyst can navigate them.

00:01:01.232 --> 00:01:05.715
Typical areas include administration, source logs, raw collection, working notes, analysis,

00:01:05.715 --> 00:01:06.938
reports, and exports.

00:01:06.938 --> 00:01:10.606
Access permissions and retention may differ across these areas.

00:01:10.606 --> 00:01:12.236
Case organization protects reasoning.

00:01:12.236 --> 00:01:17.942
It lets reviewers see whether a judgment rests on independent evidence or repeated copies,

00:01:17.942 --> 00:01:20.794
whether dates align, and where uncertainty remains.

00:01:20.794 --> 00:01:26.500
Good structure is not clerical overhead; it is part of analytical quality and accountability.
